msgid "Using Qute"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can use the xref:./qute.adoc[Qute templating engine] in your JBang "
"script by adding the `quarkus-qute` dependency.\n"
"You also need to include the `templates` directory in the script:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If your `templates` directory includes sub-directories, use `templates/="
"templates/**/*` instead."
msgstr ""

msgid "Conclusion"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you want to get started with Quarkus or write something quickly, Quarkus "
"Scripting with jbang lets you do that. No Maven, no Gradle - just a Java "
"file. In this guide we outlined the very basics on using Quarkus with JBang; "
"if you want to learn more about what JBang can do, go see https://jbang.dev."
msgstr ""
